Cell["\<\
Coordinates: the paper's polar angle theta is traded for x defined by cos \
theta = -x, so theta: 0->pi corresponds to x: -1->+1 with dx = sin theta \
dtheta (no orientation flip). Every metric function is then rational in (r, \
x) -- no trig function ever enters the computation, which turns minute-scale \
simplifications into split-second ones. Conversion rules to and from the \
paper's theta are stored in the final section, \"Comparison with the paper\".\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f4ad01e-628a-4f09-9b0d-6f8fcf87445a"],

