Cell["\<\
Horizon, eq. (2.6): r+ is the largest root of Q with 0 < r+ < 1/alpha \
(outside the r = 0 singularity, inside the conformal boundary). Q(r+) = 0 is \
linear in m; the rule m2rp expresses m through r+ and round-trips to zero. \
The Solve runs with $Assumptions neutralised -- the entry's chart-scalar \
assumptions can otherwise make Solve return {} silently.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a79d149-e080-4f56-82a6-4b24721b53fd"],

