Cell["\<\
Conical structure, read off the STORED metric components (P, Q still \
symbolic). On surfaces of constant t and r the induced metric is N dx^2 + W \
dphi^2 with N = g_xx, W = g_phiphi. W has simple zeros at the poles (first \
two entries below). Near a simple zero the circumference-to-proper-radius \
ratio tends to c Dphi with c^2 = W'^2/(4 N W) evaluated at the pole -- a \
Sqrt-free rational expression, no assumptions needed. The result is c+- = \
P(+-1) = P+-: the deficit angles are 2pi(1 - P+- Dphi/2pi), eq. (2.8)/(2.10).\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"86659eda-c209-43ac-b42e-b488041a03db"],

