Cell["\<\
P+ - P- = 4alpham (first entry): when alpham != 0 no single Dphi smooths both \
poles -- the constant-(t,r) surface can never be S^2. Choosing Dphi = \
2pi/(n-P-) = 2pi/(n+P+) with coprime positive integers n+- yields deficits \
2pi(1 - 1/n+-): the spindle WCP^1_[n-,n+]. The rule `spindle` solves the two \
conditions for Dphi and m; under it alpham = Xi(n- - n+)/(2(n- + n+)) (second \
entry) -- nonzero acceleration corresponds exactly to n- != n+.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c29e094-43aa-4657-a11f-0132752d2030"],

