Cell["\<\
The electrostatic potential, paper eq. (3.36). Phi_H is the generator \
contracted with the gauge field at the horizon, again constant there. \
Phi_infinity is the x-independent (zero mode) part of the same contraction on \
the boundary gauge field; in the gauge inherited from section 2 the boundary \
gauge field is odd in x and integrates to zero over the spindle, so \
Phi_infinity vanishes and Phi_e = -Phi_H. The magnetic potential follows by \
the electric-magnetic duality e <-> g, as the paper notes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9c45edb-a60c-47c7-b8b4-2631f5ba7f7d"],

