Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Entropy", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0859f858-31a9-496d-8557-fabdc0eacbd8"],

Cell["\<\
The Bekenstein-Hawking entropy, paper eq. (3.31). The horizon is the surface \
r = rp at constant time; its induced metric is the angular block of the \
stored metric components. In the x chart the determinant of that block is \
((rp^2 + a^2)/H^2)^2 -- a PERFECT SQUARE and a rational function, so the area \
element is rational and the integral over the spindle is elementary. In the \
polar-angle chart the same integrand is an unintegrable Sqrt of a \
trigonometric rational; this is the clearest single payoff of the coordinate \
change.

The azimuthal integration contributes the range Delta phi, and x runs over \
the full spindle from pole to pole.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f75ffb6-c872-4858-9373-a1f68a605a65"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"angBlock", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"garr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"garr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"garr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"garr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
           RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", 
     "/.", " ", "funcrule"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r", "[", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "rp"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"detAng", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Det", "[", "angBlock", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", "m2rpR"}], " ", "//",
     " ", "Simplify"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FactorSquareFree", "[", "detAng", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[91]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a0123c20-cb80-418d-abb1-cb4a8275e9ae"],

